label("5",(.4*D)+(.6*F),SW);
label("\tiny{$120^{\circ}$}",D+(1.8,0.8));
[/asy] Thanks to SAS Similarity, we see that $\triangle ABC \sim \triangle DEF.$

Therefore, we have that: \begin{align*}
\frac{AB}{BC} &= \frac{DE}{EF} \\
\frac{AB}{3\text{ cm}} &= \frac{14\text{ cm}}{6\text{ cm}} \\
AB &= \frac{14\text{ cm}\cdot3\text{ cm}}{6\text{ cm}} = \boxed{7}\text{ cm}.
\end{align*}

Note that $\dfrac{7}{16}$ and $\dfrac{16}{7}$ are reciprocals. Since $(a \times b)^n = a^n \times b^n$, we get \begin{align*}
\left(\dfrac{7}{16}\right)^{111}\times \left(\dfrac{16}{7}\right)^{111} &= \left(\dfrac{7}{16}\times\dfrac{16}{7}\right)^{111} \\
&= 1^{111} = \boxed{1}.
\end{align*}

